      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "So let's make sure we also validate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 6.99,
          "en": "those user inputs when submitting them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.99,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "And for that, to achieve this, I'll first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 12.993,
          "en": "of all add a new method here to NewExpense state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "And this could be named submitForm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 21.033,
          "en": "or submitExpenseData, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "And it should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "whenever this button at the bottom here is pressed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 27.723,
          "en": "this one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 32.1,
          "en": "Here, instead of printing some dummy values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 37.053,
          "en": "I want to trigger submitExpenseData by pointing at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "And inside of submitExpenseData, we now have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "to validate the data selected by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 49.05,
          "en": "For that we can use a if statement about which we learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "before in the course already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "and check if titleController.text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 58.47,
          "en": "after trimming it, which is a built-in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.47,
          "end": 60.87,
          "en": "that simply removes excess white space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 63.15,
          "en": "at the beginning or end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.15,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "If this is then empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "and isEmpty is a built-in property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "just as trim is a built-in method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 74.28,
          "en": "Trim can be called on strings and text is a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "and isEmpty can be called on lists and strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 80.19,
          "en": "And the result of calling trim is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 82.623,
          "en": "which is why we can use isEmpty here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 87.21000000000001,
          "en": "So this overall will be true if we have an empty title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.21000000000001,
          "end": 89.043,
          "en": "or just a bunch of blanks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.51,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "And if that's the case, then we wanna show an error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "which we'll do soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "But of course that's not the only case when we wanna show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 105.03,
          "en": "Instead, we also wanna show an error message if we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.03,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "an invalid amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "Now the amount is not just invalid if it's empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "but also if it, for example, is a text that doesn't qualify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "as a number or if it's a number smaller than zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "because our amounts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 122.643,
          "en": "for the expenses here must be greater than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 126.48,
          "en": "Therefore, as a first step, we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.48,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "to transform the amountController.text, which we get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 134.103,
          "en": "which is always a string, to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "So our enteredAmount as we could call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 142.47,
          "en": "has to be a number, not a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.47,
          "end": 145.17000000000002,
          "en": "And this transformation can be achieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.17000000000002,
          "end": 150.17000000000002,
          "en": "by using double.tryParse, a method built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "tryParse takes a string as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 160.02,
          "en": "and then returns a double if it is able to convert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.02,
          "end": 162.9,
          "en": "that string to a number, to a double",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.9,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "or it returns null if it's not able to convert it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "So using tryParse on a text like 'Hello'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 172.173,
          "en": "Would yield null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.04,
          "end": 178.04,
          "en": "For example, tryParse on something like 1.12",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "as a string would yield 1.12",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 182.223,
          "en": "as a double, as a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "So that's something we have to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "And with that done, we can add another variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 192.153,
          "en": "which could be called amountIsInvalid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 199.953,
          "en": "which we wanna set equal to true or false, so to a Boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 204.21,
          "en": "But of course we don't wanna hard code true or false here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 206.61,
          "en": "Instead that should be derived dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.61,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "by taking a look at enteredAmount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.913,
          "en": "Just as we're taking a look at the title text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.9,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "So what we wanna check here is whether enteredAmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "is maybe equal to null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 222.81,
          "en": "because I just mentioned tryParse will yield null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.81,
          "end": 224.76,
          "en": "if an invalid number was entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.76,
          "end": 228.32999999999998,
          "en": "So some text that can't be converted to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.32999999999998,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "So now amountIsInvalid will be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "if enteredAmount is null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 235.71,
          "en": "because indeed then the amount is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 238.95,
          "en": "But that's not the only case in which we would consider it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.95,
          "end": 241.38,
          "en": "invalid in this app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.38,
          "end": 243.57,
          "en": "Instead, the amount will also be invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 246.39,
          "en": "if it's smaller than zero as mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.39,
          "end": 250.26,
          "en": "So here we actually wanna derive true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.26,
          "end": 253.14,
          "en": "based on a combination of conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.14,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "And in Dart, you can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 257.94,
          "en": "with two very important operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.94,
          "end": 261.24,
          "en": "The logical and operator, which is written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.24,
          "end": 266.04,
          "en": "with two ampersand symbols, or the logical",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.04,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "or operator which is written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 270.933,
          "en": "with two pipe symbols.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.83,
          "end": 273.99,
          "en": "And you will see this in many other programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.99,
          "end": 275.313,
          "en": "languages as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "Of course thus far you already saw some operators like plus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 284.25,
          "en": "or minus, which are used in mathematical operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.25,
          "end": 288.33,
          "en": "There also would be the asterisk operator for multiplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.33,
          "end": 291.72,
          "en": "or the forward slash operator for division.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.72,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "But where plus and minus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.52,
          "en": "and so on are used to derive numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.52,
          "end": 300.033,
          "en": "and and or are used to derive Booleans.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 302.85,
          "en": "And they help us derive Booleans",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.85,
          "end": 305.52,
          "en": "by combining multiple conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 308.97,
          "en": "Here, the first condition is that enteredAmount is equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 308.97,
          "end": 313.05,
          "en": "to null, in that case amountIsInvalid will be true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 317.01,
          "en": "or it should also be true if enteredAmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.01,
          "end": 320.373,
          "en": "is smaller or equal than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.84,
          "end": 324.673,
          "en": "So if one of these two conditions is met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 324.673,
          "end": 326.673,
          "en": "amountIsInvalid, will be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 332.46,
          "en": "If both conditions are false, amountIsInvalid is false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 332.46,
          "end": 334.47,
          "en": "but it is enough that one of them is met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.47,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "to set amountIsInvalid to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 339.783,
          "en": "because of this logical or operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 341.37,
          "end": 343.488,
          "en": "Well, and with that, we now know when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.488,
          "end": 345.51,
          "en": "amountIsInvalid will be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.51,
          "end": 348.27,
          "en": "We can now add this here to our if condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.27,
          "end": 351.93,
          "en": "where we're checking whether the title is invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 351.93,
          "end": 353.97,
          "en": "with this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 353.97,
          "end": 357.99,
          "en": "Now we wanna combine this condition with amountIsInvalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.99,
          "end": 362.31,
          "en": "by again using the or operator, the or operator instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 363.75,
          "en": "of the and operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 363.75,
          "end": 366.93,
          "en": "because we wanna make it into this if block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 366.93,
          "end": 369.84,
          "en": "where we wanna show an error message in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 373.62,
          "en": "if at least one of our checks yields through.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 373.62,
          "end": 377.7,
          "en": "Because even if all the input values are valid, it's enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 377.7,
          "end": 382.14,
          "en": "for one input value to be invalid to show an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 382.14,
          "end": 385.47,
          "en": "because we need all input values to be valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 385.47,
          "end": 386.823,
          "en": "not most of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 388.14,
          "end": 392.34000000000003,
          "en": "So therefore here we want to now add amountIsInvalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 392.34000000000003,
          "end": 394.59000000000003,
          "en": "And this is now of course not a condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 394.59000000000003,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "but it is a value that contains true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 399.84000000000003,
          "en": "And that's all the if statement wants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.84000000000003,
          "end": 403.17,
          "en": "It wants a bunch of true or false values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 403.17,
          "end": 405.54,
          "en": "or expressions that yield true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.54,
          "end": 408.27,
          "en": "or false to know whether the code inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.27,
          "end": 410.58299999999997,
          "en": "of the if statement should be executed or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.51,
          "end": 414.42,
          "en": "So we spent quite some time on this if statement already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 414.42,
          "end": 417.63,
          "en": "but it is important to understand how if statements work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 417.63,
          "end": 420.93,
          "en": "and how these conditions work and how they can be combined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 420.93,
          "end": 423.48,
          "en": "And we're of course also still not done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 423.48,
          "end": 425.88,
          "en": "because the date could of course also be invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 425.88,
